' The body of services.puml / services-dark.puml. Not a diagram on its own: it
' carries no start marker, so PlantUML will not render this file directly.
'
' Careful: the start and end markers must not appear in this file at all, not
' even inside a comment. PlantUML scans for them lexically, so a comment naming
' one opens a second diagram here and the include fails with a line number
' pointing at neither file. See README.md.
'
' Split out because the README ships a light and a dark render of this diagram
' and the two must not drift. Every colour is a variable the wrapper supplies,
' so the dark render is dark throughout rather than a dark canvas behind white
' cards, which is worse than shipping no dark render at all.
'
' The post-render passes in README.md are not optional for either half.

' A post-render step widens this single font name into a fallback stack, so a
' viewer without Inter gets a sans-serif rather than the monospace a missing
' font can fall back to.
skinparam defaultFontName Inter

' $n_ink is the *name* of the control-plane line colour, not the colour. The
' dark wrapper brightens that line to near-white, so a legend hard-coding
' "black" would describe a light grey line as black in half the renders.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title Services, grouped by the protocol they speak to a client

header
<b>FOUR PLANES, GROUPED BY PROTOCOL.</b>  Control is Mumble-over-TCP through the gateway.
Realtime is UDP or WebRTC <b>straight to the service</b>.  Bulk and admin are plain HTTP.
The gateway routes on the <b>16-bit type in the frame header</b> and never parses a payload, so a new service is a TOML block, not a release.
Shard keys: <b>scaling.puml</b>.   Gateway internals: <b>gateway-internals.puml</b>.   Rationale: <b>ARCHITECTURE.md</b>.
endheader

actor "legacy Mumble\nclient" as legacy $c_neutral
actor "Fancy client" as fancy $c_blue
actor "**operator**" as oper $c_purple
cloud "**publist.mumble.info**\nthe public server list" as publist $c_indigo

component "**gateway**\nTLS · framing · rate limit\n**single writer per client socket**\nroutes by type, config-driven" as gw $c_gw

database "**session store**\n«gateway infrastructure, not a service»\nsequence number + bounded replay ring\nno client, no message type, no tier\n--\n**«not built»: the ring is in-process**, so it does\nnot outlive a pod and RESUME cannot cross one" as sstore $c_gw2

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**control plane**, gRPC only; no client reaches these directly" as CTRL $c_faint {

  package "essential, down means nobody logs in" as ESS $c_ess {
    component "**session-lifecycle**\nVersion · Authenticate · Reject\nServerSync · CodecVersion\nCryptSetup · Ping · timeout sweep\n--\n**UserState (9)**, moves, self-mute,\nmoderator mute/deafen, priority\nspeaker, registration\n**UserStats (22)**, uptime, idle,\nclient build, certificate\n«both were routed to userdata,\nwhich had no handler for either»\n0,2,3,4,5,**9**,15,21,**22** + **1000**" as slife $c_hub
    component "**session-view**\nthe composed live view of\nevery connected session.\nThe whole domain reads here.\nOwns nothing, writes nothing.\n**no client-facing type**" as sview $c_hub
    component "**permissions**\nACL eval\n+ request coalescing\n12,13,20 + **1001**" as perms $c_card
    component "**metadata**\nchannels · tree\nmembership\n6,7 + **1002**" as meta $c_card
    component "**userdata**\nprofiles · accounts · blobs\n**SuperUser is account 0**, so a\nguest is `None`, never `0`\n**no password ⇒ not claimable**\n**by name alone**\n14,18,23 + **1003**" as users $c_card
    component "**server-config**\nruntime-mutable,\nper server instance\n24,25 + **1013**" as scfg $c_card
  }

  package "core: a feature dies" as CORE $c_core {
    component "**text**\nhistory: **UUIDv7**\n11 + **1005**" as text $c_card
    component "**pchat**\nE2EE · key mgmt\nhistory: **UUIDv7**\n**1006**" as pchat $c_card
    component "**moderation**\nbans · kicks\n«UserRemove 8 is a kick or a ban,\nso it is moderation's, not userdata's»\n--\nchecked on the **root** channel:\nremoval is from the server, not\na room. `Ban` to ban, `Ban` **or**\n`Kick` to kick. Keyed to **address**\n**and certificate**, either alone\nis trivially evaded\n8,10 + **1007**" as mod $c_card
  }

  package "optional, nobody notices" as OPT $c_green {
    component "**plugins**  26 + **1010**\n**push** «FCM»  **1011**\n**audit** «UUIDv7»  **1012**\n**onboarding**  **1014**\n**social**  **1015**\n· reactions · receipts · typing\n· polls · watch · whiteboard\n**link-preview**  **1016**\n**context-actions**  16,17 + **1017**" as opt $c_card
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**realtime plane**, UDP / WebRTC, client connects **directly**" as RT $c_ess {
  component "**voice**  «core»\n**mints the ciphers** · answers the ping\nUDP 64738, its own socket\n1 (tunnel), 19 + **1004**\n--\nOpus **forwarded, never transcoded**\npayloads refcounted, never copied\n--\naudio routes both ways: a datagram on its own\nsocket, or **UDPTunnel** through the gateway for\na UDP-blocked client. Membership is read from a\n`session-view` subscription, never asked per packet\n--\n**«not built»**: whisper/shout, `VoiceTarget` (19)\nis still a stub, so only channel speech routes" as voice $c_card
  component "**screenshare**  «optional»\nsignalling only\n**1008**\n--\n**«not built»: no SFU.** There is no str0m\ndependency; media has nowhere to go" as share $c_card
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**HTTP plane**, plain HTTPS, client connects **directly**" as HTTP $c_green {
  component "**files / http**  «optional»\nsigned URLs · uploads · blobs\nplugin binaries · audit exports\n**1009**" as files $c_card
  component "**operator-api**  «admin»\nREST + OpenAPI\nauth **pluggable**: OIDC · JWT\nmTLS · token\ndefault **off**, localhost-bound" as opapi $c_purple
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**outward plane**, this server talking about itself" as OUT $c_indigo {
  component "**directory**  «optional»\nhourly announcement to the\npublic Mumble server list\n--\n**no client, no wire type, no endpoint**\nnothing dials it; it dials out" as dirsvc $c_card
}

' ══════════════════════ control: TCP through the gateway ═══════════════════
legacy -[$l_ink]-> gw : **TCP 64738**\nTLS + framing
fancy  -[$l_ink]-> gw : **TCP 64738**\n+ **zstd** stream «not built»

gw -[$l_blue]-> CTRL  : gRPC
gw -[$l_blue]-> RT : gRPC, signalling\nand UDPTunnel only
gw -[$l_blue]-> files : gRPC, mint a signed URL
note on link $c_blue
  Payload forwarded **verbatim**, already protobuf, never
  re-encoded. A **local socket** when co-located, a Unix socket,
  or a named pipe on Windows, and TCP when not.
  **Circuit breaker per service**, inbound shed by `tier`.
  **RESUME**: a sequence number per session, so a rolling deploy
  is not 10 000 simultaneous full floods. **«not built»**: the
  ring is in-process, so it does not survive the pod it is in.
end note

gw -[$l_amber]-> sstore : stamp · replay
note on link $c_gw2
  **Why this is not in a tier.** `tier` decides what the gateway does
  when a dependency is down, and both answers are wrong here:
  **essential** would reject logins over a lost *optimisation*, and
  **optional** claims nobody notices, false, because its absence
  bites at the worst possible moment and the resulting herd can
  saturate metadata, which *is* essential.
  It is not a service at all: no client reaches it, it has no
  message type, and it is never scaled on its own. It is the
  gateway's own durable state, externalised so a pod can die.
  **Legacy clients can never RESUME**, so staggered drain and
  jittered reconnect hints are required regardless. This store
  optimises a path that must already survive without it, which is
  what "not essential" means.
  It is reported in readiness as a **warning**, never as unready.
end note

' ══════════════════════ realtime: no gateway hop ═══════════════════════════
legacy -[$l_red]-> voice : **UDP 64738**
fancy  -[$l_red]-> voice : **UDP 64738**
note on link $c_ess
  Same port, different protocol, **different process**, murmur
  binds these separately, Server.cpp:125 vs 193. So audio never
  traverses the gateway. Only UDPTunnel, the UDP-blocked
  fallback, comes through the control plane.
  **Affinity is by channel, never by client.**
  Per-packet cost is **N seals, not one**: every listener needs
  the frame under their own key.
end note

fancy -[$l_red]-> share : **WebRTC / ICE**
note on link $c_ess
  Media direct to the SFU; only signalling via the gateway.
  str0m is **ICE-lite**: it ignores trickled candidates, its own
  rides in the SDP answer. Never trickle ICE through the control
  plane, and retry offers until answered.
end note

' ══════════════════════ HTTP: bulk and admin ═══════════════════════════════
fancy  -[$l_green]-> files : **HTTPS**, signed URL
legacy -[$l_green]-> files : **HTTPS**
oper   -[$l_purple]-> opapi : **HTTPS + REST**

' ══════════════════════ outward: the only edge that leaves ═════════════════
dirsvc -[$l_indigo]-> publist : **HTTPS POST**, hourly
note on link $c_indigo
  The only connection Starling **opens** to the internet, and the
  only place it publishes anything about itself. Authenticated by
  the server's **own TLS certificate as a client certificate**, so
  the list keys an entry to the same fingerprint clients pin and
  nobody can update somebody else's listing.
  Refused unless the operator set a name, a secret and a URL, and
  **never** for a password-protected server, a public list is a
  directory of servers people can join. Both rules are murmur's.
  The count comes from **session-view**, not from a gateway: with
  two gateways either one sees a fraction.
end note

legacy -[$l_red].-> voice : **UDP ping**, unauthenticated
note on link $c_ess
  How a server browser measures a server it has never connected
  to: version, users, limits. Answered from the packet path, so
  the numbers are **pushed in on a timer**, a fetch per ping
  would make an open UDP port a lever on session-view.
  murmur's `allowping` gates **this** ping only. Gating the
  connectivity ping a connected peer sends would silently push
  every client onto tunnelled audio.
end note

' ══════════════════════ the two halves of session ══════════════════════════
slife -[$l_blue].-> sview : session up · down · moved · flags
slife -[$l_blue]-> voice : mint a CryptSetup payload
note on link $c_ess
  **Voice mints the key, because voice is what uses it** to seal
  UDP. Key material never crosses a service boundary; a
  client-requested resync takes the same path.
end note

' ══════════════════════ session-view is the edge for the domain ════════════
CORE -[$l_blue].-> sview : **one** composed snapshot stream
OPT  -[$l_blue].-> sview
RT   -[$l_blue].-> sview
gw   -[$l_blue].-> sview
note on link $c_hub
  **Read here and nowhere else**, otherwise every service depends
  on four others, with four caches each to keep warm.
  It **forwards but never decides**, and is a
  **subscription hub, not a proxy**, nothing on the audio path
  makes a request.
  **Every mailbox is bounded**, with a shed policy.
end note

sview -[$l_blue].-> users : profile changes
sview -[$l_blue].-> perms : groups + current-channel perms
sview -[$l_blue].-> meta  : channel · tree · membership
sview -[$l_blue].-> scfg  : limits · bandwidth

note bottom of sview $c_hub
  **A stale deny is safe; a stale grant is a security bug.**
  A revocation invalidates the view before it is acknowledged;
  a grant may arrive lazily.
end note

opapi -[$l_purple]-> ESS : gRPC, **operator** context
note on link $c_purple
  **The one thing that does not read through session-view**, and
  must not: that view is of *connected* users, while an operator
  edits registered accounts, offline bans and config.
  No service accepts an unauthenticated call.
  **Fail closed on audit.**
end note

note as OPLOG $c_gw2
  **The operator log, every service writes it, no service owns it.**
  Distinct from `tracing`, which is a developer's dial and defaults
  to `warn`. This is the record an operator keeps, **who connected,**
  **what was refused, what an administrator changed**, categorised
  (server · session · channel · message · permission · security ·
  plugin · admin) and levelled independently of `RUST_LOG`.
  Configured under `[logging]`, written by a **dedicated OS thread**
  behind a bounded queue so a slow disk cannot stall the voice path,
  and **overflow is counted, never silent**.
  It is not on this diagram as a component because it is not one:
  every service holds a handle, and the writer is process-wide.
end note

note bottom of ESS $c_card
  **Each service owns its own schema.** No service reads
  another's tables. One migration tool, many schemas.
  Built: `sqlx` over the `Any` driver, so the backend is chosen
  by URL scheme, **SQLite, MySQL or PostgreSQL**. With no
  `[storage]` block a service gets its own SQLite file named
  after it, under the shared data directory.
  Twelve services keep one: userdata, metadata, server-config,
  text, pchat, moderation, audit, push, files, plugins,
  onboarding, permissions. The rest hold no durable state at all.
  `permissions` is the newest, and the one whose store is
  **optional**: it starts without one and says so, because an
  unreachable database must not mean an unauthorised server.
end note

legend bottom
|= line |= plane |= transport |
| <color:$l_ink>**$n_ink**</color> | control | Mumble over TCP+TLS, through the gateway, ordered per client |
| <color:$l_red>**red**</color> | realtime | UDP or WebRTC, **direct to the service** |
| <color:$l_green>**green**</color> | bulk | HTTPS, signed URL, out of band |
| <color:$l_purple>**purple**</color> | admin | HTTPS + REST in, gRPC out, pluggable auth, default off |
| <color:$l_indigo>**indigo**</color> | outward | HTTPS out to the public server list, the only edge Starling opens |
| <color:$l_blue>**blue**</color> | internal | gRPC, solid is a call, dotted is a cached subscription |
Anything marked **«not built»** is drawn because the design depends on it, and
labelled because it does not exist yet. See `README.md` in this directory.
endlegend
